.SH 1
Machine Learning in ABC Mapper: Random Forest Implementation Report
.LP
This report outlines the recent modifications made to the ABC synthesis
tool\(cqs mapping phase to integrate an ML-based heuristic
(specifically, a small Multi-Class Random Forest classifier) for
determining cut survival during technology mapping.
.SH 2
1. What We Did
.LP
We extended the traditional ABC \f[CR]map\f[R] command (technology
mapper) to dynamically select which cuts are retained dynamically using
Machine Learning instead of using standard static heuristics like
absolute dominance or constant cut volume limitations.
.PP
To achieve this: - We modified the internal representation of cuts to
log various cut topology features (size, max depth, logic level, etc.)
and labeled them based on whether they would \(lqsurvive\(rq under
strict algorithmic structural heuristics (dominance and volume).
- We generated and captured testing data using varying
\f[CR]ABC_CUT_HEURISTIC\f[R] runs.
- We designed a lightweight Python training pipeline exclusively
focusing on a Random Forest classifier.
- We directly transformed the small trained Random Forest decision trees
into inference code (\f[CR]ml_inference.h\f[R]), so that ABC natively
executes ML predictions at C-level without heavy external ML inference
dependencies (like TensorFlow or ONNX runtime).
.SH 2
2. Dataset Collection & Heuristics Used
.LP
The dataset was gathered by executing ABC across multiple testbench
designs (\f[CR].blif\f[R] files in \f[CR]blif_files/\f[R]) by explicitly
executing \f[CR]run_experiments.sh\f[R].
.PP
To gather supervised training labels and feature profiles, we initially
leveraged three traditional \(lqscore\(rq heuristics: 1.
\f[B]Dominance\f[R]: Prioritizes preserving cuts if they are not totally
dominated structurally by other identical subsets of the logic cone.
Handled using logical subset checking.
2.
\f[B]Volume\f[R]: Handled cuts heavily based on overall logical breadth;
specifically simulating survival if the cut has 4 or fewer leaf nodes
(\f[CR]nLeaves <= 4\f[R]).
3.
\f[B]Random\f[R]: An arbitrary parity-based heuristic to keep \(ti50%
random cuts and trivially simple 1-leaf cuts.
Used purely as a comparative baseline.
.PP
For each mapping node, \f[CR]cuts_all_features.csv\f[R] dumped extracted
model features, and \f[CR]cuts_survivors.csv\f[R] boolean outcomes based
on the heuristics above.
We combined the survivability values to construct labels reflecting the
relative \(lqquality\(rq of a cut.
.SH 2
3. Features Extracted (\f[CB]X\f[B])
.LP
We generated the header logic by extracting specific mathematical and
topological features per cut.
The feature vector array (\f[CR]float features[9]\f[R]) includes: -
\f[CR]nLeaves\f[R]: Total number of leaf variables.
- \f[CR]nVolume\f[R]: An approximate measurement of the internal mapping
subset logic volume.
- \f[CR]max_level\f[R]: Maximum circuit propagation depth.
- \f[CR]avg_level\f[R]: Aggregated average depth across all leaf inputs.
- \f[CR]random_val\f[R]: Baseline uniform distribution values appended
for normalization/validation parity checks.
- \f[CR]uTruth\f[R]: The raw truth table signature (integer).
- \f[CR]uTruth_popcount\f[R]: Structural bit-count complexity of the
boolean truth expression.
- \f[CR]max_leaf_refs\f[R]: Total external graph references per leaf
variable.
- \f[CR]max_arrival\f[R]: The locally estimated worst-latency signal
arrival times.
.SH 2
4. Modeling Strategy and Training
.LP
We opted explicitly for a \f[B]Multi-Class Random Forest Classifier\f[R]
implemented via Python\(cqs \f[CR]scikit-learn\f[R] taking into account
the balance between rapid inference cycle execution in C natively vs
model complexity.
.PP
\f[B]Model Particulars:\f[R] - \f[B]Estimators
(\f[CB]n_estimators\f[B])\f[R]: 15 decision trees.
- \f[B]Depth (\f[CB]max_depth\f[B])\f[R]: Strict ceiling of 8 steps to
enforce quick bounded runtime.
- \f[B]Classes\f[R]: 3 output classes (\f[CR]0=Poor\f[R],
\f[CR]1=Average\f[R], \f[CR]2=Good\f[R]), synthesized respectively by
blending dominance logic and maximum volume sizes
(\f[CR]score = s_dom + s_vol\f[R]).
Training leveraged \f[CR]class_weight=\(aqbalanced\(aq\f[R].
.PP
During execution, \f[CR]train_model.py\f[R] reads the feature dataset,
trains \f[CR]RandomForestClassifier\f[R], measures classification
accuracy against the targets, and recursively translates each estimator
tree structure directly through an abstract syntax translator block into
inline \f[CR]if/else\f[R] boundaries encapsulated in standard
\f[CR]C\f[R] functions.
.SH 2
5. Main Extracted Base Modifications
.LP
Deep structural interventions were introduced inside
\f[CR]src/map/mapper/\f[R]:
.IP \(bu 3
\f[B]\f[CB]mapperCut.c\f[B]\f[R]: We inserted a feature extraction and
dataset logging routine, \f[CR]Map_CutMLDump\f[R], which computes max
levels, total arrivals, logic signatures, etc., right \f[I]before\f[R]
standard native dominance filtering (\f[CR]Map_CutFilter\f[R]).
We modified \f[CR]Map_CutFilter\f[R]\(cqs main routine to allow
\f[CR]ABC_CUT_HEURISTIC\f[R] overrides (e.g.\ bypassing filtering
constraints and strictly allowing Volume or Random filtering based on
runtime arguments).
.IP \(bu 3
\f[B]\f[CB]mapperCore.c\f[B]\f[R]: Captured exact end-stage metrics upon
mapping termination by storing final area (\f[CR]AreaFinal\f[R]), delay
(\f[CR]fRequiredGlo\f[R]), and tracking exactly how many total mapping
permutations naturally survived filtering logic into
\f[CR]cuts_qor.csv\f[R].
.IP \(bu 3
\f[B]\f[CB]mapperInt.h\f[B]\f[R]: Modified \f[CR]Map_CutStruct_t_\f[R]
internal framework to contain an intrinsic mapping string integer
\f[CR]cut_id\f[R] per cut structure layout to natively cross-reference
data across our multi-pass data collection loops reliably.
.IP \(bu 3
\f[B]\f[CB]mapperCutUtils.c\f[B]\f[R]: Dynamically allocated sequential
unique \f[CR]cut_id\f[R] properties inside memory pool management via
\f[CR]Map_CutAlloc\f[R].
.HLINE
.PP
\f[B]Summary\f[R]: We substituted hardcoded technology map pruning paths
with a robust, data-conscious mechanism mapping feature relationships.
By employing small-scale, balanced Random Forest logic integrated at the
ground-level core logic (via C-header injection strategy), ABC
accurately balances complex graph traversal while keeping mapping
compute operations constrained.
.pdfsync
